window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-b9f9668068e928e8"]={"key":"ny_b1-b9f9668068e928e8","group":"ny_b1","uid":"b9f9668068e928e8","rank":8,"title":"gdpval tooling recovery sequence ballantry 001","occupation":"buyers_purchasing_agents","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re the manufacturing buyer at Ballantry Utilities, supporting the recovery of production tooling from Glassmere Press after its administrator took control on Friday. Eleven Ballantry-owned die sets remain on the supplier’s floor, and Meera Stavropoulos needs a decision-ready recovery plan before she signs the administrator’s access agreement. The plan will be used by Imani Rosenthal, a transport planner who has not handled an insolvency retrieval before, and Selma Zamora, a quality engineer who understands tooling approval but was not in the recovery meeting. It must let both readers coordinate the work without turning into a tutorial or implying that purchasing can approve insurance, customs, transport safety, or production release. Use these planning facts: the sets are D01–D11; D08–D11 require customs release; D03 is oversized and must travel alone; and the other sets may travel two at a time. One low-loader is available, and a collection occupies it for eight hours including loading, travel, and unloading, so it can make only one collection in an access window. The administrator is offering access from 06:00 to 16:00 on 10, 12, 17, and 19 December 2025 and 13 and 14 January 2026. Customs release is expected at 08:00 on 16 December, with a downside assumption of 08:00 on 19 December. The insurer requires written notification to be acknowledged before any die is loaded; acknowledgement is targeted for 9 December but has not yet been received. Ballantry’s receiving plant, accredited layout laboratory, and proving press are closed from 22 December through 12 January inclusive. Outside that closure, the laboratory can sign off one set per weekday, with its report available at 16:00, and the proving press can process one set per weekday only after layout sign-off, no earlier than the next working day. D01–D03 are needed for line restart on 13 January, D04–D07 by 16 January, and D08–D11 by 23 January. Prepare two files: `tooling_recovery_plan.docx`, limited to five pages total including appendices, and `tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx`. Write both files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames. I need the package to cover seven things: (1) show one baseline sequence for all eleven sets from release at Glassmere Press through receipt, layout, proving, and readiness for use, with dates and handoffs that respect the shared-resource limits; (2) make the insurance acknowledgement, customs release, administrator access, plant shutdown, laboratory capacity, and press capacity visible as conditions rather than background commentary; (3) distinguish the expected customs timing from the downside case and show what changes if the expected timing is missed; (4) identify where the sequence stops being capable of meeting each production need date, including the assumptions behind those breakpoints; (5) give Imani and Selma concrete owners, decision points, and timing for the transport and quality handoffs while marking matters that require confirmation by the relevant specialist; (6) include the controls needed to identify, collect, receive, preserve, inspect, and prove the tooling without treating collection or a satisfactory-looking proof part as automatic production release; and (7) keep the Word plan and the set-level spreadsheet consistent on every shared set, date, dependency, status, scenario, and production need date. Present the facts and executable sequence without advising Meera whether to sign the access agreement and without inventing costs, insurance cover, customs clearance, permits, test results, or approvals that have not been given.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `tooling_recovery_plan.docx` — A concise, decision-ready tooling recovery sequencing plan for the transport and quality users. (Must be no more than five pages total, including appendices.; Must cover all eleven die sets and the baseline and downside planning cases.; Must be usable by the named transport and quality readers without overstepping purchasing authority.; Must agree with tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx on all shared facts and figures.)\n- `tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx` — An executable set-level schedule showing dates, dependencies, resource use, gates, handoffs, and scenario effects. (Must account for D01 through D11 exactly once in the baseline sequence.; Must make resource capacity and predecessor relationships auditable.; Must distinguish baseline assumptions from the customs downside case.; Must agree with tooling_recovery_plan.docx on all shared facts and figures.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/tooling_recovery_plan.docx","bytes":39962,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/41bdf8b58d88f73b766ec686f8e0f77546b879efe56dde55b684ab3daf65e534.docx","sha256":"41bdf8b58d88f73b766ec686f8e0f77546b879efe56dde55b684ab3daf65e534","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Ballantry Utilities\nGlassmere Press Tooling Recovery Plan\nIssue basis: planning sequence for Meera Stavropoulos | 05-Dec-2025 planning cut | Buyer coordinates; specialists approve\n1. Decision-useful conditions\nThis memo sets out one executable baseline for the eleven Ballantry-owned dies. It does not recommend signing or refusing the administrator access agreement. Dates marked “forecast” remain conditional until the named specialist evidence is received.\nCondition / fact\nBaseline planning treatment\nOwner / evidence\nAdministrator access\nOnly 06:00–16:00 on 10, 12, 17, 19 Dec; 13, 14 Jan. One 8-hour low-loader trip per window.\nAdministrator confirms window; buyer issues trip pack.\nInsurance\nWritten notification acknowledgement is a load predecessor; 09-Dec target is not acknowledgement.\nInsurer acknowledgement to buyer before loading.\nCustoms\nD08–D11 load only after written release. Expected 16-Dec 08:00; downside 19-Dec 08:00.\nCustoms specialist supplies release evidence.\nShutdown / capacity\nPlant, lab and press closed 22-Dec–12-Jan inclusive. Outside closure lab = 1 set/weekday; press = 1 set/weekday, next working day after layout.\nPlant owner confirms reopening; Selma controls slots.\n2. Baseline sequence and handoffs\nThe workbook is the controlling set register; the sequence below is its readable handoff view. “Ready” means formal quality/production disposition after proving—not collection, receipt, or a satisfactory-looking part.\nTrip / sets\nAccess & collection\nReceipt\nLayout / report\nProving\nForecast ready\nNeed / status\nT1 • D01, D02\n10-Dec; two standard\n10-Dec\nD01 11-Dec / 16:00; D02 12-Dec / 16:00\nD01 12-Dec; D02 15-Dec\nD01 12-Dec; D02 15-Dec\n13-Jan / on time\nT2 • D03\n12-Dec; oversized alone\n12-Dec\n15-Dec / 16:00\n16-Dec\n16-Dec\n13-Jan / on time\nT3 • D04, D05\n17-Dec; two standard\n17-Dec\nD04 17-Dec; D05 18-Dec / 16:00\nD04 18-Dec; D05 19-Dec\nD04 18-Dec; D05 19-Dec\n16-Jan / on time\nT4 • D06, D07\n19-Dec; two standard\n20-Dec quarantine\nD06 13-Jan; D07 14-Jan / 16:00\nD06 14-Jan; D07 15-Jan\nD06 15-Jan; D07 16-Jan\n16-Jan / zero float\nT5 • D08, D09\n13-Jan; customs release required\n13-Jan\nD08 15-Jan; D09 16-Jan / 16:00\nD08 16-Jan; D09 19-Jan\nD08 16-Jan; D09 19-Jan\n23-Jan / expected customs\nT6 • D10, D11\n14-Jan; customs release required\n14-Jan\nD10 19-Jan; D11 20-Jan / 16:00\nD10 20-Jan; D11 21-Jan\nD10 20-Jan; D11 21-Jan\n23-Jan / expected customs\nHandoff rhythm: Imani receives the trip pack and confirms route, lifting/rigging competence, restraint, equipment suitability, unloading slot, and (for D03) route/permit with the relevant specialists. Selma receives the receipt record and reserves one laboratory and one press slot per weekday; her quality/production disposition is the release gate. Purchasing coordinates and records decisions but does not approve insurance, customs, transport safety, or production release.\n3. Customs downside and breakpoints\nExpected case: written release at 08:00 on 16-Dec supports the conditional January T5/T6 loads. Downside case: release at 08:00 on 19-Dec leaves D08–D11 on HOLD for the 13/14-Jan windows; there is no later offered administrator window, so their 23-Jan need becomes unattainable unless an additional access window is confirmed. The workbook flags this branch on every customs-controlled row.\nInsurance: acknowledgement later than 09-Dec 16:00 loses T1; later access windows are already allocated, exposing D01–D03 restart timing.\nAccess: missing T3 (17-Dec) or T4 (19-Dec) leaves D04–D07 without a permitted pre-shutdown collection and exposes the 16-Jan need.\nQuality: D06 and D07 consume the first two reopening lab slots (13/14-Jan); a missed slot or press day removes the available float to 16-Jan.\nEvery trip: before departure, the administrator or authorized site representative signs the release/custody record. Identity and condition are checked and photographed at Glassmere and rechecked at receipt.\n4. Control path and exceptions\nSupplier release → transport → controlled receipt\nBuyer issues an asset list and trip pack. At Glassmere, the carrier and administrator verify die ID against the list, photograph condition, record seal/packaging and exceptions, and obtain signed custody acknowledgement before departure. Transport/lifting specialists confirm competent lifting and rigging, load restraint, equipment suitability, and D03 route/permit; those are confirmations, not buyer approvals. Receiving confirms an unloading slot, handling capacity, secure quarantine/storage, and preservation against damage or deterioration while work is pending.\nQuality release is a separate chain\nReceiving inspection and identity/condition recheck → accredited layout verification (report at 16:00) → proving on the next working day → assessment against the approved inspection basis → formal quality/production disposition. A collected die or good-looking proof part is not automatically released for production.\nException rule\nFor damage, mismatch, failed layout, or failed proving: Selma/quality places the die and record on HOLD, segregates it in quarantine, captures photographs and the nonconformance evidence, names the disposition owner, and blocks production release. Buyer updates the schedule only after the responsible specialist records a disposition; transport or customs issues remain with those specialists.\n5. Set register (reconciliation key)\nAll eleven sets appear exactly once below; customs-controlled sets are D08–D11 and D03 is oversized. The spreadsheet carries the same classifications, dates, need-date groupings, and baseline completion status.\nSets\nClass\nCustoms\nNeed date\nBaseline status\nD01–D02\nStandard\nNo\n13-Jan-2026\nForecast on time (conditional gates)\nD03\nOversized\nNo\n13-Jan-2026\nForecast on time (conditional gates)\nD04–D07\nStandard\nNo\n16-Jan-2026\nForecast on time (D06–D07 zero float)\nD08–D11\nStandard\nYes\n23-Jan-2026\nForecast on time (expected customs case)\nSource of truth: tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx, “Recovery Schedule”. Planning assumptions are not approvals or operational commitments.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx","bytes":8708,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/4934c9b19b9b687bb7dbf339aa7a2a326a558437f6665c41e2b23881f3ea27c6.xlsx","sha256":"4934c9b19b9b687bb7dbf339aa7a2a326a558437f6665c41e2b23881f3ea27c6","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Recovery Schedule","row_count":28,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Ballantry Utilities | Glassmere Press tooling recovery"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Baseline is conditional: insurer acknowledgement is targeted 09-Dec-2025 and still pending at issue. Customs release is expected 16-Dec (downside 19-Dec)."]},{"r":"3","cells":["Access windows: 06:00–16:00 on 10, 12, 17, 19 Dec 2025 and 13, 14 Jan 2026. One 8-hour low-loader trip per window; max two standard sets, D03 alone."]},{"r":"5","cells":["Set","Class","Customs","Need date","Trip","Access window","Collection / load","Receipt","Layout slot","Layout report","Proving","Forecast ready","Predecessors / hold points","Primary handoff owner","Required evidence","Baseline status","Customs downside"]},{"r":"6","cells":["D01","Standard","No","46035","T1","46001","46001","46001","46002","46002.66666666666","46003","46003","Insurance ack; access; transport readiness","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (conditional gates)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"7","cells":["D02","Standard","No","46035","T1","46001","46001","46001","46003","46003.66666666666","46006","46006","Insurance ack; access; transport readiness","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (conditional gates)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"8","cells":["D03","Oversized","No","46035","T2","46003","46003","46003","46006","46006.66666666666","46007","46007","Insurance ack; access; route/permit; lift plan","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; route confirmation; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (conditional gates)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"9","cells":["D04","Standard","No","46038","T3","46008","46008","46008","46008","46008.66666666666","46009","46009","Insurance ack; access; transport readiness","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (conditional gates)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"10","cells":["D05","Standard","No","46038","T3","46008","46008","46008","46009","46009.66666666666","46010","46010","Insurance ack; access; transport readiness","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (conditional gates)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"11","cells":["D06","Standard","No","46038","T4","46010","46010","46011","46035","46035.66666666666","46036","46037","Insurance ack; access; transport readiness; plant reopens","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; quarantine receipt; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (zero float after reopen)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"12","cells":["D07","Standard","No","46038","T4","46010","46010","46011","46036","46036.66666666666","46037","46038","Insurance ack; access; transport readiness; plant reopens","Buyer / transport / quality","Signed custody; photos; quarantine receipt; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (zero float)","Not affected by customs branch"]},{"r":"13","cells":["D08","Standard","Yes","46045","T5","46035","46035","46035","46037","46037.66666666666","46038","46038","Insurance ack; access; written customs release (expected 16-Dec)","Buyer / customs / transport / quality","Customs release; signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (expected customs case)","If release only 19-Dec: HOLD Jan load; no later offered access (need date unattainable without added window)"]},{"r":"14","cells":["D09","Standard","Yes","46045","T5","46035","46035","46035","46038","46038.66666666666","46041","46041","Insurance ack; access; written customs release (expected 16-Dec)","Buyer / customs / transport / quality","Customs release; signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (expected customs case)","If release only 19-Dec: HOLD Jan load; no later offered access (need date unattainable without added window)"]},{"r":"15","cells":["D10","Standard","Yes","46045","T6","46036","46036","46036","46041","46041.66666666666","46042","46042","Insurance ack; access; written customs release (expected 16-Dec)","Buyer / customs / transport / quality","Customs release; signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (expected customs case)","If release only 19-Dec: HOLD Jan load; no later offered access (need date unattainable without added window)"]},{"r":"16","cells":["D11","Standard","Yes","46045","T6","46036","46036","46036","46042","46042.66666666666","46043","46043","Insurance ack; access; written customs release (expected 16-Dec)","Buyer / customs / transport / quality","Customs release; signed custody; photos; receipt check; layout report; proof assessment","Forecast on time (expected customs case)","If release only 19-Dec: HOLD Jan load; no later offered access (need date unattainable without added window)"]},{"r":"18","cells":["Control register"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Insurance","Written acknowledgement must be received and acknowledged before any die is loaded; target 09-Dec is not confirmation.","","","","","","","","","","","Insurer / buyer","Hold loading","","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["Customs","D08–D11 require written release. Expected 16-Dec 08:00; downside 19-Dec 08:00.","","","","","","","","","","","Customs specialist","Hold affected loading","","",""]},{"r":"21","cells":["Administrator access","Only listed 06:00–16:00 windows; site release record and signed custody acknowledgement required before departure.","","","","","","","","","","","Administrator / buyer","Gate each trip","","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["Transport","Transport planner confirms competent lifting/rigging, restraint, equipment suitability, and D03 route/permit; buyer coordinates only.","","","","","","","","","","","Imani / transport specialist","Hold load","","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["Receiving","Plant confirms unloading slot, handling capacity, secure quarantine/storage, and preservation before arrival.","","","","","","","","","","","Receiving / buyer","Hold dispatch","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["Quality","Receipt inspection, accredited layout, proving, assessment to approved basis, then formal production disposition; proof part is not release.","","","","","","","","","","","Selma / quality and production","Release gate","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Shutdown","Receiving, laboratory and press closed 22-Dec through 12-Jan inclusive.","","","","","","","","","","","Plant owner","No site work","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["Breakpoint logic"]},{"r":"28","cells":["• Insurance: acknowledgement later than 09-Dec 16:00 loses the 10-Dec trip; D01–D03 restart need dates are then exposed because later windows are already allocated."]},{"r":"29","cells":["• Non-customs access: missing 17-Dec or 19-Dec collection leaves D04–D07 without a permitted pre-shutdown trip; their 16-Jan need is unattainable without a new window."]},{"r":"30","cells":["• Quality: D06 layout 13-Jan and D07 layout 14-Jan are the zero-float restart slots; losing either lab/press slot threatens 16-Jan."]},{"r":"31","cells":["• Customs downside: release at 19-Dec 08:00 is too late to make the 13/14-Jan loads conditional; with no later offered access, D08–D11 cannot meet 23-Jan absent an added window."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The baseline accounts for every die set D01–D11 exactly once, without omission, duplication, or substitution, and identifies D03 as oversized and D08–D11 as customs-controlled.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Set-level schedule and corresponding coverage in the Word plan.","grader_hint":"Enumerate the unique set identifiers in the baseline schedule and compare them with D01–D11. Confirm that the special handling and customs classifications are attached to the correct sets."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each set has a coherent end-to-end chain from supplier release or collection through receipt, layout sign-off, proving, and a readiness disposition, with every dated successor later than its required predecessor.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Set-level milestones, predecessor fields, and plan narrative.","grader_hint":"Trace several sets, including D03 and at least one customs-controlled set. Layout cannot precede receipt, proving must be no earlier than the working day after layout, and readiness cannot precede the stated quality disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The collection sequence never assigns more than one low-loader trip to an access window, carries no more than two standard sets per trip, and carries D03 alone.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Collection dates, trip groupings, and resource assignments in the schedule.","grader_hint":"Group collection rows by access date. There may be only one trip on each date; each trip may contain at most two sets, except that any trip containing D03 must contain no other set."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All planned collections fall within the offered access dates of 10, 12, 17, and 19 December 2025 or 13 and 14 January 2026, and the plan does not treat general site access as available outside those windows.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Collection schedule, assumptions, and access-gate descriptions.","grader_hint":"Compare every collection date with the six permitted dates and inspect the prose for any contradictory implication of unrestricted access."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No customs-controlled set is shown as loadable before written customs release, and the expected and downside release timings are represented as conditional scenario facts rather than completed clearance.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Customs gate, scenario logic, and D08–D11 collection dependencies.","grader_hint":"Confirm that D08–D11 depend on written release and that the workbook models 08:00 on 16 December as expected and 08:00 on 19 December as downside. The artifact must not claim customs release has already occurred."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Written insurer acknowledgement is a predecessor hold point for every loading activity, with the targeted 9 December acknowledgement clearly distinguished from an actual acknowledgement.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Gate register or dependency fields and the Word plan.","grader_hint":"Verify that no trip is authorized merely because notification was sent or targeted. The plan should name acknowledgement as the evidence required to release loading."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No receipt, layout, or proving work is scheduled at the receiving plant during the 22 December 2025 through 12 January 2026 closure, and the restart effect is visible.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule dates, shutdown marker, and recovery narrative.","grader_hint":"Inspect all receiving-plant activities for dates inside the inclusive closure. Site collection may occur only on offered dates, but plant receipt and quality work must respect the closure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Laboratory and press assignments respect one set per weekday for each resource, and proving for a set occurs no earlier than the next working day after its layout report becomes available at 16:00.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Per-set layout and proving dates plus any resource-loading view.","grader_hint":"Count unique sets assigned to each resource on every date and test the lag between layout and proving. Exclude weekends and the stated shutdown when determining the next working day."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Readiness dates are compared with the correct production requirements: D01–D03 by 13 January, D04–D07 by 16 January, and D08–D11 by 23 January, with any miss or zero-float exposure made explicit.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Need-date, forecast-readiness, and variance or status information in both artifacts.","grader_hint":"For each set, compare forecast readiness with its applicable need date. A set is not on time merely because it has been collected or proved without a release disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The customs downside case changes the affected sequence, fallback load choice, or available float in a logically traceable way rather than appearing only as a risk note.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario-specific rows, dates, conditional branch, or quantified impact.","grader_hint":"Look for an executable response to the release moving from 16 December to 08:00 on 19 December. The consequence must be connected to actual trips or downstream dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The plan identifies the material breakpoints at which a missed acknowledgement, customs release, access window, collection, layout slot, or press slot would make a production need date unattainable or materially exposed, and states the assumptions supporting those breakpoints.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Breakpoint, float, exception, or decision-point content in the Word plan and schedule.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the breakpoints are derived from the sequence rather than generic warnings. They should let a coordinator tell when recovery action or escalation is still useful."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recovery controls require a documented release and handover at the supplier site, including custody acknowledgement by an authorized site representative or administrator before departure.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Collection or handover controls in the Word plan.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent language requiring a release record, collection note, or signed custody transfer. Mere possession of an access appointment is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The plan requires identity and condition verification against the asset or die identifier before loading and again on receipt, supported by an exception record and suitable condition evidence such as photographs.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-collection and receipt controls.","grader_hint":"Look for positive identity matching and condition capture at both ends, not only a generic instruction to inspect the tooling."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Transport readiness addresses competent lifting or rigging, load restraint, equipment suitability, and route or permit confirmation for the oversized die without purporting to approve those matters.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transport prerequisites and ownership statements.","grader_hint":"Credit a concise set of hold points assigned to the transport or lifting specialist. The buyer should not self-certify legal, engineering, or safety compliance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Receiving readiness includes a confirmed unloading slot, suitable handling capacity, a secure quarantine or storage location, and preservation against damage or deterioration while quality work is pending.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Receiving and preservation handoff content.","grader_hint":"The artifact should prevent a collected die arriving without capacity or a controlled location. Generic wording such as 'receive tooling' does not satisfy the criterion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The quality path distinguishes receipt inspection, accredited layout verification, press proving, assessment against an approved part or inspection basis, and formal production-release disposition.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Quality sequence in the plan and milestone definitions in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Confirm that these are distinct controls and that collection, visual condition, or a seemingly acceptable proof part is not equated with production release."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The plan gives a usable exception path for damage, identity mismatch, failed layout, or failed proving, including segregation or hold status, evidence capture, ownership, and prevention of unintended release.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception or nonconformance treatment in the Word plan and status vocabulary in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Credit a compact common exception path. It must do more than say 'escalate' and should preserve the affected die and its records pending disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Functional boundaries are explicit: purchasing coordinates the sequence, while insurer acknowledgement, customs release, transport and lifting suitability, and quality or production release remain decisions or confirmations of the appropriate specialists.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner, authority, and hold-point language throughout the plan.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the document is operational without making unsupported approvals. Naming a specialist owner and required evidence is sufficient; explaining specialist procedures is unnecessary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A transport planner unfamiliar with insolvency retrieval and a quality engineer absent from the meeting can independently understand the sequence, conditions, handoffs, and exception triggers without the document becoming a general tutorial.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall usability, definitions, and information hierarchy of both artifacts.","grader_hint":"Assess whether essential local context and brief definitions are present while elementary purchasing, logistics, or metrology instruction is avoided."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered Word document is no more than five pages total, including appendices, and remains readable at normal viewing size.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count and visual inspection of tooling_recovery_plan.docx.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX to PDF and count all pages. Reject attempts to meet the cap through illegibly small text, clipped tables, or content placed outside the printable page."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Word plan and workbook contain the same eleven set identifiers, customs classification, production need-date grouping, and baseline completion status.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-file comparison of the set register and summary statements.","grader_hint":"Extract the shared set-level facts from both deliverables and compare them. Summary aggregation in the Word plan is acceptable if it remains reconcilable to the workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every collection, layout, proving, readiness, gate, and scenario date stated in the Word plan agrees with the corresponding date in the workbook.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-file comparison of all shared dates and scenario labels.","grader_hint":"Sample every date printed in the Word plan and trace it to the workbook, then inspect the workbook for material schedule dates contradicted by the narrative."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Actions and handoffs have an accountable function or named participant, a due time or triggering event, required evidence, and a clear recipient or next owner sufficient for execution.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action, handoff, gate, or responsibility content in both artifacts.","grader_hint":"Look for executable assignments rather than a list of concerns. Owners may be functions where no named individual was provided, but invented personal names should not be necessary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package clearly separates stated facts, planning assumptions, pending confirmations, and actual approvals or results, presents an executable sequence, and does not advise whether the access agreement should be signed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Status language, assumptions, conclusions, and overall presentation across both files.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a reader could mistake a target, forecast, or dependency for a completed approval. The package may show conditions relevant to Meera's decision but must stop short of recommending signature or refusal."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Ballantry Utilities must recover production dies from an insolvent stamping supplier through restricted access windows while transport, customs, insurance, laboratory, press, and shutdown constraints compete. The work must bridge purchasing, logistics, and quality for readers with different levels of recovery experience.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling six access windows with one low-loader, an oversized single-load set, and eleven total die sets.","Sequencing receipt, constrained laboratory work, constrained press proving, and formal readiness around a three-week shutdown.","Propagating expected and downside customs timing through a feasible collection and quality schedule.","Making cross-functional handoffs executable for readers with different backgrounds without overstepping purchasing authority.","Keeping a concise Word plan and an auditable set-level workbook consistent."],"authoring_plan":{"design_intent":"Construct a reference solution consisting of a concise recovery plan and a set-level workbook that demonstrate one feasible baseline, a meaningful customs downside branch, and clear boundaries between procurement coordination and specialist approval. No reference files are supplied.","scenario_constraints_to_preserve":["Account for all eleven tooling sets exactly once in the baseline.","One oversized set travels alone; each other trip carries no more than two sets.","Only one eight-hour low-loader trip may occur in each administrator access window.","Four customs-controlled sets require written release before loading. Model both the expected release and the later downside release as assumptions, not achieved facts.","Written insurer acknowledgement is a universal predecessor to loading and remains pending at plan issue.","Receiving, layout, and proving cannot occur during the stated plant shutdown.","Layout and proving each have capacity of one set per weekday. A set cannot be proved until the next working day after its layout report.","Readiness means completion of the quality disposition, not merely collection or proving."],"gold_relationships":["For every set: collection date must be an offered access date; receipt is not earlier than collection; layout is not earlier than receipt; proving is at least the next available working day after layout; readiness is not earlier than proving and disposition.","For every trip: the low-loader trip count per access date is at most one; standard-set count is at most two; a trip containing the oversized set contains exactly that set.","For customs-controlled tooling: loading is conditional on written customs release, and scenario changes must propagate to collection opportunities and downstream float.","For all tooling: loading is conditional on acknowledged insurer notification.","For each resource and working date: laboratory assignments are at most one and press assignments are at most one.","On-time status is determined by comparing formal readiness with the applicable production need date.","Any breakpoint or last-responsible date must be derivable from remaining access windows, shutdown periods, predecessor lags, resource capacities, and production need dates.","Every fact shared by the document and workbook must reconcile exactly."],"professional_content_expected":["Supplier-site release, identity check, condition evidence, signed custody handover, and preservation of records.","Competent lifting and rigging, load restraint, equipment suitability, oversized-load route or permit confirmation, and receiving capability as specialist-confirmed hold points.","Controlled receipt, identity and condition recheck, secure quarantine or storage, and preservation while approval is pending.","Distinct receipt inspection, accredited layout verification, press proving, comparison with an approved inspection basis, and formal release disposition.","A nonconformance path covering mismatch, damage, failed layout, and failed proving, with hold status, evidence, ownership, and blocked release.","Functional ownership that coordinates work without asserting insurance, customs, transport-safety, quality, or production authority.","Brief contextual definitions and explicit handoffs sufficient for readers who were not in the meeting, without general training material."],"workbook_behavior":["The workbook should permit audit of each set's scenario, trip, milestones, predecessors, owner, evidence or gate status, need date, forecast readiness, and timing exposure.","Resource loading and date logic should reveal any double booking or invalid predecessor sequence.","The downside case should alter an executable branch or timing consequence rather than duplicate the baseline with a narrative warning."],"intended_verdict":"A strong solution is feasible under the stated capacities, keeps the production need dates visible, shows exactly where limited float is consumed, and gives logistics and quality users sufficient handoff detail to execute while preserving specialist approval boundaries. A superficially polished chronology that omits custody, quality release, resource capacity, scenario propagation, or cross-file reconciliation should not pass as strong work."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"recovery_plan","filename":"tooling_recovery_plan.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise, decision-ready tooling recovery sequencing plan for the transport and quality users.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be no more than five pages total, including appendices.","Must cover all eleven die sets and the baseline and downside planning cases.","Must be usable by the named transport and quality readers without overstepping purchasing authority.","Must agree with tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx on all shared facts and figures."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"recovery_schedule","filename":"tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"An executable set-level schedule showing dates, dependencies, resource use, gates, handoffs, and scenario effects.","required":true,"constraints":["Must account for D01 through D11 exactly once in the baseline sequence.","Must make resource capacity and predecessor relationships auditable.","Must distinguish baseline assumptions from the customs downside case.","Must agree with tooling_recovery_plan.docx on all shared facts and figures."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"buyers_purchasing_agents","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":6.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"A manufacturing procurement reviewer should validate schedule feasibility and purchasing controls, with a quality or tooling reviewer checking the inspection, proving, nonconformance, and release boundaries. Cross-file reconciliation should be performed mechanically where possible and visually confirmed after rendering.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The calendar, capacity, customs, insurance, and production dates are planning assumptions supplied for the scenario rather than verified operational commitments.","More than one feasible set ordering may satisfy the constraints; grading therefore tests relationships, capacity, controls, and consistency rather than a single literal schedule.","The work does not determine actual customs, insurance, transport, lifting, metrology, or production-release approval."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:26:29+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:26:29+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:26:29+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:26:29+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R09', 'R20']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:26:29+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/b9f9668068e928e8","declared_deliverables":["tooling_recovery_plan.docx","tooling_recovery_schedule.xlsx"]};
